-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_hookio_stream_wideread.adam - the wide input side of System.HookIO
  from C (PaskalCPP's std_hookio TestStreamWideRead, with Adam's ccs=
  cases)

  The C fixture's wide read sequences (std_hookio_c_wideread's 12
  variants: fgetwc, getwc, fgetws, ungetwc, orientation, long reads,
  unmappable and cut-off bytes, seeks, CR runs, Ctrl-Z) under the "C" and
  ".UTF8" locales, on a handle over a memory IO holding the variant's
  sample (std_hookio_c_wrsample) and on a real file of the same bytes: in
  r, rb and rt as pcpp's row, then in the three ccs= text modes (UTF-8:
  lowio's UTF-8 read, a character cut by a fill, ftell's walk over the raw
  bytes; UTF-16LE: lowio's wide translation; UNICODE: ANSI with no BOM).
  Every step's value, errno, ferror, fwide and ftell equal the real
  file's. ucrt clears a descriptor's UTF-8 read state (utf8translations,
  startpos) only when its slot is first made (osfinfo.cpp), so a UTF-8
  open inherits the last file's; a handle is a fresh descriptor, so each
  real run starts on a slot a 1-byte ASCII UTF-8 read left fresh (the
  fixture's std_hookio_c_freshfh does the same before a ccs= row's open).
  One line per sample and per case: ok when every check of it held, else
  a FAIL line per check that did not.
*******************************************************************************/

/*
